Subject: [PATCH 13/13] SDL: ask Emscripten for a canvas with no alpha channel

PPSSPP draws its UI, the browser shows it, and every consumer of the canvas
that is not the browser's own compositor sees nothing at all. Round 26 is the
measurement: a screenshot of the tab has 1552 distinct colours in it, while the
smoke harness reading the same canvas four times a second finds 0 opaque pixels
and 1 colour across 481 samples.

The context attributes the same round reported say why:

    {"alpha":true, "premultipliedAlpha":true, "depth":true, "stencil":true, ...}

A WebGL drawing buffer with an alpha channel is composited against the page as
premultiplied data. PPSSPP never writes alpha into the backbuffer, so the buffer
holds the picture in RGB with alpha at 0 everywhere, and the two readings follow
from that one fact:

  - on screen, `dst = src.rgb + page.rgb * (1 - 0)` — the picture is *added* to
    the page and looks perfect;
  - anywhere else, `drawImage` into a transparent target gives `src.rgb` at
    alpha 0, and `getImageData` un-premultiplies that back to (0,0,0,0).

Which of those a host gets depends only on whether it composites the canvas
itself. Embedding this canvas in a page of its own — which is what this package
is for — lands on the second one.

Established rather than argued, and without an emulator round: tests/fakes/
now holds two fakes that differ in one argument, the alpha they clear with.
`draws/` (alpha 1) is read directly by the sampler; `transparent/` (alpha 0)
reproduces round 26's fingerprint exactly — a screenshot with colour in it, 0
opaque pixels, and the same picture recovered when the sampler draws the canvas
over an opaque backdrop. Both run in the same browser, in the same SwiftShader,
through the same drawImage, so the sampler and the browser are both exonerated
and the alpha channel is not.

SDL3 defaults SDL_GL_ALPHA_SIZE to 8, and src/video/emscripten/SDL_emscriptenopengles.c
passes `_this->gl_config.alpha_size > 0` straight into the WebGL context
attributes. Asking for 0 is therefore the whole fix, and it belongs here rather
than in the harness: forcing the attribute where the instrument creates its
context would turn the smoke run green while everything this package ships
stayed invisible.

Emscripten-only. A desktop window has no page behind it to be transparent
against, and nothing in PPSSPP wants a see-through one.

diff --git a/SDL/SDLMain.cpp b/SDL/SDLMain.cpp
index a15c732fd..2ae7ccd6d 100644
--- a/SDL/SDLMain.cpp
+++ b/SDL/SDLMain.cpp
@@ -1852,6 +1852,20 @@
 	SDL_GL_SetAttribute(SDL_GL_DEPTH_SIZE, 24);
 	SDL_GL_SetAttribute(SDL_GL_STENCIL_SIZE, 8);
 	SDL_GL_SetAttribute(SDL_GL_DOUBLEBUFFER, 1);
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+	// A WebGL drawing buffer with an alpha channel is composited *against the page*, and
+	// the browser treats it as premultiplied. PPSSPP does not write alpha into the
+	// backbuffer, so every pixel arrives with alpha 0 and colour in RGB: putting that on
+	// screen is `src.rgb + page.rgb`, which looks perfect, while anything else that reads
+	// the canvas — drawImage, toDataURL, a host compositing it into its own page — gets
+	// `src.rgb` at alpha 0 and un-premultiplies it back to nothing.
+	//
+	// SDL3 defaults SDL_GL_ALPHA_SIZE to 8 and its Emscripten driver passes
+	// `alpha_size > 0` straight to the WebGL context attributes, so asking for zero here
+	// is what gives this canvas an opaque drawing buffer. Nothing else in PPSSPP wants a
+	// see-through window.
+	SDL_GL_SetAttribute(SDL_GL_ALPHA_SIZE, 0);
+#endif
 
 	// Force fullscreen if the resolution is too low to run windowed.
 	if (g_DesktopWidth < 480 * 2 && g_DesktopHeight < 272 * 2) {
